@--[11]. As it is the Lord alone who instructs...

@5088. "(Joseph) ministered to them" = that he instructed them.

@5120[4]. To "give to drink with a cup of water in My name" = to instruct in the truths of faith from a very little charity.

@5126[3]. From childhood to adolescence a communication is opened to the interior Natural... by means of instruction by parents and masters...

@5201. "They fed in the sedge" = instruction... in scientifics...

@--. To "pasture" = to be instructed. @--[2], Illustrated.

@--[3]. "Shepherds" = those who instruct; and "flock" = those who are being instructed.

@5280[4]. So far as they allow, all do indeed begin to be reformed by instruction in the truths and goods of spiritual life...

@5342[3]. Truths give quality to good... and therefore from this age (of adolescence) he is imbued with truths by means of instructions...

