@--[5]. To be "educated upon scarlet" = to be instructed from infancy in the good of mutual love from the Word.

@9755[4]. To "tread the sea with horses," when said of Jehovah, = to instruct the natural man, who possesses scientifics.

@9857[4]. To "instruct him in the way of judgment" (Isaiah 40:14) = to render knowing, intelligent, and wise.

@10225. The second state (of man) is from the fifth up to the twentieth year. This state is a state of instruction and knowledge, and is called childhood. @--[4], Explained.

@10280. "Thou shalt speak to the sons of Israel, saying" = instruction for those who are of the Church... To "speak," and to "say, "when by Jehovah, = instruction. References.

@10283[7]. That however they are instructed concerning good and truth, still they will not receive. Signified.

@--[8]. "Not to pasture them" = not to instruct and reform.

@10525. "Jehovah spake to Moses" = instruction concerning the quality of worship and of the Church with the Israelitish nation.

