@--. They at once flee to interpretations; such as these...

@4790. The things which are primary for interpretation. Signified, Explained. @4966.

@4966. The primary things for interpretation are those things which primarily conduce to interpret the Word; and thus to understand the doctrinal things of love to God and of charity towards the neighbour which are from the Word.

@5084. (Sensuous things rejected) by the things which are primary for interpretation. Signified, Explained.

@5087. The Celestial of the Natural taught them from the primary things for interpretation. Signified, Explained.

@5093. "Each one according to the interpretation of his dream" (Genesis 40:5) = the event which they had in themselves; (for) "the interpretation of a dream" = the explication, and thence the Knowledge of the event.

@5105. "There is no interpreter of it" (Genesis 40:8) = that no one knows what is in these things. (For) "an interpretation" = the explication of what it has in itself.

@5107. "Are not interpretations with God?" (Genesis 40:8) = that the Divine is in them. (For) "an interpretation," when predicated of dreams, = that which is in them.

@5121. "This is the interpretation thereof" (Genesis 40:12) = revelation from perception... of what it had in itself. Explained.

@5141. "That he had interpreted good" (Genesis 40:16) = what would happen.

@5151. "This is the interpretation thereof" (Genesis 40:18) = what it had in itself.

@5168. "As Joseph had interpreted to them" (Genesis 40:22) = prediction by the Celestial in the Natural. To "interpret" = to say what it has in itself, or what is in it, and also what will happen, thus to predict.

@5180[2]. The rest they interpret well.

@5225. "And no one interpreting these things to Pharaoh" (Genesis 41:8) = that it was unknown what would happen. To "interpret" = to know what will happen.

@5235. "Each according to the interpretation of his dream..." (Genesis 41:11) = what would happen to each.

@5253. "And no one interprets it" (Genesis 41:15) = ignorance of what was in it.

@5478. "Because there was an interpreter between them" (Genesis 42:23) = that spiritual things are then apprehended quite differently... For an interpreter translates the language of one into the language of another, thus he expounds the meaning of one to the apprehension of another...

@5620[13]. Because (the literal sense) suffers itself to be explicated by interpretations in everyone's favour; but not the internal sense...

@6620. They admit nothing but the literal sense, which they interpret in favour of their own principles and cupidities...

