@AE 714[29]. So that it may also be translated that... @--[end].

@DeVerbo 7[7]. To interpret the Word as to its spiritual sense from falsities of doctrine, closes Heaven.

Interrogate.; Interrogare.
Interrogation.; Interrogatio.

@AC 226. (Why the Lord inquires of man what He already knows). @1931. @5800[end]. @6132.

@2693. In the sense of the letter, this is an interrogation by the Lord; but, in the internal sense, it is the infinite perception of all things.

@3179. "Let us ask her mouth" (Genesis 24:57) = ... to perceive whether she consents.

@3291. "She went to ask Jehovah" (Genesis 25:22) = a state of communication. To "ask," when said of the Lord, = to be communicated...

@3385. To "ask" (Genesis 26:7) = to diligently inquire -disquirere-.

@4295. "Jacob asked and said..." (Genesis 32:29). @4296.

