@4889. "He asked the men of that place" (Genesis 38:21) = that truths were consulted. To "ask" = to consult.

@5597. "The man in asking asked about us" (Genesis 43:7) = that he clearly perceived the things which were in the Natural. To "ask" = to perceive another's thought... because in Heaven there is a communication of all thoughts, insomuch that no one has need to ask another what he is thinking. @5800.

@5677. "He asked them as to peace" (Genesis 43:27) = a perception that it is well. To "ask" = to perceive another's thoughts.

@6250. For in the internal sense an interrogation denotes Knowledge from perception.

@8081. "It shall be that thy son shall ask thee" (Exodus 13:14) = perception from the truth which is of conscience. (For) to "ask" = Knowledge from perception.

@8665. "They asked a man his companion as to peace" (Exodus 18:7) = a mutual Divine celestial state. Explained.

@10548. To "interrogate Jehovah" (Exodus 33:7) = to be instructed concerning the truths and goods of the Church and of worship; for all interrogation of Jehovah is done for the sake of instruction concerning these things.

@HH 214[end]. The less wise interrogate the more wise; and these the Lord...

@526[4]. To the inquiry about Abraham... they replied...

@AR 376. The will to interrogate. Signified.

