Inundate.; Inundare.
Inundation.; Inundatio.
See <Flood>.

@AC 645. Preservation from the inundation of cupidities. Signified, Explained.

@705[2]. The Lord Himself calls temptations "an inundation" (Luke 6:48). Illustrated.

@--[3]. False principles... which inundate man, as they did the Antediluvians.

@756[2]. Their phantasies... and cupidities... are like inundations and exhalations...

@757. Temptations as to voluntary things... can never be separated from temptations as to intellectual things. If they were separated there would not be any temptation, but an inundation such as there is with those who live in the fires of cupidities...

@--[2]. They are called "the cataracts of heaven" from being an inundation of falsities or of reasonings.

@790. Inundations of waters = desolations and temptations, which involve the same as falsities; for desolations and temptations are nothing but inundations of the falsities excited by evil Spirits...

@2240[2]. "An inundating stream" (Jeremiah 47:2) = falsity.

@3542[2]. "An inundating river" (Isaiah 30:28) = falsity thus overflowing.

@4423[2]. Then they who are of the old Church, who are thus removed from Heaven, are in a kind of inundation as to the interiors, and in fact in an inundation over head. The man himself does not perceive this inundation while he lives in the body, but he comes into it after death. This inundation manifestly appears in the other life... like a foggy mist with which they are begirt, and by it they are separated from Heaven. The state of those who are in this foggy mist is that they cannot at all see what the truth of faith is, and still less what is its good; for the light of Heaven... cannot penetrate into this mist. This is the state of a vastated Church. @4424[end].

@4843[4]. Therefore both temptations and vastations are signified and described by inundations of waters and floods.

@5585[5]. "The inundation of anger" (Isaiah 54:8) = temptation. @6997[4].

@5725. It has been given to know from experience what an inundation or flood is in the spiritual sense. This inundation is twofold; one which is of cupidities, and the other which is of Falsities. That which is of cupidities is of the voluntary part, and is of the right side of the brain; whereas that which is of Falsities is of the intellectual part, in which is the left side of the brain. When a man who has lived in good is remitted into his proprium, thus into the sphere of his own life, there then appears as it were an inundation; and when he is in this inundation, he is indignant, is angry, thinks restlessly, desires vehemently. It is one thing when the left side of the brain, where falsities are, is inundated; and it is another thing when the right side, where evils are, is inundated.

@--[2]. But when man is kept in the sphere of life which he has received from the Lord through regeneration, he is completely outside such an inundation... It has been given me to perceive that I was outside the inundation, and this for a considerable time, during which I saw that other Spirits were in it. Afterwards, however, I was myself immersed, and then I apperceived the likeness of an inundation. In such are they who are in temptations. (Continued. See <Flood>.) @SE 4155.

@6015[4]. "An inundating stream" = what is scientific destroying the understanding of truth, and thus laying it waste.

@6385[5]. It is predicted that the Churches will be "inundated and penetrated" by falsities from evils at the time of the end. @AE 514[14].

@7553[4]. "An inundation" = immersion in falsities, and thus the vastation of truth. References.

@--. "An inundation of hail" (Isaiah 28:2) = the destruction of truth through falsities.

@NJHD 196. These assaults are made in various ways; by an influx of stumbling blocks into the thoughts and the will against truths and goods, and also by a continual bringing forth and recollection of the evils which the man has done and of the falsities which he has thought, thus by an inundation of such things...

@DFaith 53. "Which shall become an inundating stream, and they shall inundate the earth and its fulness" (Jeremiah 47:2) = the devastation by (falsities from Hell) of all things of the Church.

@AR 409[end]. By "streams" are signified temptations, because temptations are inundations of falsities.

@531[2]. When they thus... seemed to be inundated, I desired to know their lot in the deep...

@CL 267[4]. For these almost separate their spirit from its connection with the body; and, from vision, inundate the understanding...

@TCR 119[3]. The Heavens are then inundated by the evils which rise up...

@SE 4165. On an inundation of the evil.

@5411. There appeared as it were an inundation there.

@5812. On the Babylon destroyed, and the inundation...

@--[2]. At last the Last Judgment came upon them, and they were inundated as with waters... @5813.

@DMin 4768. On inundations of two kinds.

@--. (One kind of inundations which appears in the other life) is for the good, when they are inundated by the spheres of various Hells, which spheres are directed by the Lord, and they then produce anxieties and temptations. According to the state, they reach to the feet, over the feet, to the belly, to the neck, and to the head; rarely over the head.

@4768. The other kind of inundation is for the evil who are in the Hells, when they begin to be insane, and are to be repressed. Then the sphere of the celestial Heaven is let down... and wherever it comes they are as in a flood... and this with terrors and cries... Both kinds of inundations have appeared to me.

@AE 304[6]. By "hail" and its "inundation" are signified falsities which destroy the truths of the Church.

@355[21]. That to "inundate" = immersion in falsities and evils. References.

@401[17]. "An inundation of waters" = immission into falsities; "waters" = falsities; and "an inundation" = immission.

@411[11]. By "inundations of waters," in the Word, are signified temptations. @518[39].

@481[3]. "Inundation" and "heat" are mentioned when evils and falsities from proprium, and also from others who are in evil, rise up and inflow.

@504[11]. "Inundation and rain" = the irruption of falsities.

@518[34]. The destruction of the Church through falsities, is signified by "inundation by a stream".

@538[11]. As temptations come forth through inundations of evils and falsities...

@644[25]. "An inundating shower" = falsities and imaginary things in abundance rushing in. @--[26].

@--[end]. Inundations of waters = inundations of falsities, and temptations.

@684[39]. "Inundation" = the falsification of truth.

@Coro 34[2]. That falsities in a heap are described by "inundations." Illustrated.

